# Report class naming

Domain report/read-model classes are prefixed with `Report` to distinguish them from entity/aggregate classes. This applies to every module (Catalog, CustomerManagement, Ordering, Inventory, Procurement, and any new modules).

## Rules

- Any domain class that represents a report or read-model must start with the `Report` prefix.
- Example: `ReportCustomerMetrics` (CustomerManagement), not `CustomerMetrics`.
- Do not use the `Report` prefix on entities, aggregates, DTOs, commands, or queries.
- Follow this convention when creating or renaming report classes across the whole application.
